{
  "mn40:0.1": "Middle Discourses 40 ",
  "mn40:0.2": "The Shorter Discourse at Assapura ",
  "mn40:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn40:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying in the land of the Aṅgas, near the Aṅgan town named Assapura. ",
  "mn40:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "mn40:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "mn40:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn40:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn40:2.1": "“Mendicants, people label you as ascetics. ",
  "mn40:2.2": "And when they ask you what you are, you claim to be ascetics. ",
  "mn40:2.3": "Given this label and this claim, you should train like this: ‘We will practice in the way that is proper for an ascetic. That way our label will be accurate and our claim correct. ",
  "mn40:2.4": "",
  "mn40:2.5": "",
  "mn40:2.6": "The services of those whose robes, almsfood, lodgings, and medicines and supplies for the sick we enjoy shall be very fruitful and beneficial for them. And our going forth will not be barren, but will be fruitful and fertile.’ ",
  "mn40:2.7": "",
  "mn40:3.1": "And how does a mendicant not practice in the way that is proper for an ascetic? ",
  "mn40:3.2": "Any mendicant who has not given up covetousness, ill will, irritability, acrimony, disdain, contempt, jealousy, stinginess, deviousness, deceit, corrupt wishes, and wrong view ",
  "mn40:3.3": "is not practicing in the way that is proper for an ascetic, I say. And that is due to not giving up these stains, defects, and dregs of an ascetic, 